! ============================================================================
! dng-fst.dng.twol
! Two-level morphophonological rules for Dungan [dng]
!
! Dungan is analytic, ~ no morphophonemic alternation, so this
! rule set is intentionally minimal. Its main jobs are:
!   (1) realize the morpheme-boundary markers (%> and %+) as the empty string
!       on the surface, so that stem+particle concatenations surface cleanly;
!   (2) document the phonological constraint noted in the Wikipedia
!       grammar: the ў /u/ vs у /əu/ contrast and labial-context behaviour
!       (kept as a commented constraint, since the orthography is already
!       lexicalized in our stems).
!
! Source of rules: Russian Wikipedia "Дунганский язык" (Salmi 2007; 林涛 2012).
! ============================================================================

Alphabet
 ! Cyrillic letters used by Dungan
 А Б В Г Д Е Ё Ж З И Й К Л М Н О П Р С Т У Ф Х Ц Ч Ш Щ Ъ Ы Ь Э Ю Я
 а б в г д е ё ж з и й к л м н о п р с т у ф х ц ч ш щ ъ ы ь э ю я
 ! Dungan-specific Cyrillic letters
 Ә ә Ң ң Җ җ Ў ў Ү ү
 ! Boundary markers: deleted on the surface
 %>:0 %+:0
 ;

Sets
 Vowel = а е ё и о у ы э ю я ә ў ү ;
 Cons  = б в г д ж з й к л м н п р с т ф х ц ч ш щ ң җ ;
 Labial = б п м ф в ;

Definitions

Rules

! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Rule 1: The animate-plural boundary %> deletes on the surface.
!   жын%>му  ->  жынму   (人們)
! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
"Plural boundary deletion"
%>:0 <=> _ ;

! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Rule 2: The clitic boundary %+ deletes on the surface.
!   чы%+ли   ->  чыли    (吃哩)
!   ни%+ди   ->  ниди    (你的)
! These particles are written as separate orthographic units in some texts and
! joined in others; in this transducer we model them as cliticised forms whose
! boundary is invisible on the surface string.
! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
"Clitic boundary deletion"
%+:0 <=> _ ;

! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Rule 3 (DOCUMENTED, currently vacuous): ў vs у after labials.
!   Per Salmi 2007 / 林涛 2012: after labial consonants (б п м ф в) the close
!   back vowel /u/ is written у, not ў (ў /u/ otherwise contrasts with у /əu/).
!   Example of the distribution: бу 不 (/pu/, not *бў), фу 服 (/fu/, not *фў) —
!   after a labial the vowel is spelt у; ў appears in non-labial context.
!   Schematically, were the rule active: ...б%>ў... -> ...бу...
!   Because our lexicon stores already-correct orthographic stems, no rewriting
!   is required; this constraint is recorded for future productive suffixation.
!   Enable by uncommenting if/when a productive suffix introduces an underlying
!   ў in labial context.
! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
! "u after labial is written u not w"
! ў:у <=> Labial: _ ;
